      "writtenOn": "2026-09-04T09:39:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is `ldapt://` chosen specifically here?\n\nIf the purpose of this test is to verify that an invalid URL scheme is rejected, could this be parameterized with a template for different invalid schemes? Unless `ldapt://` is intended to cover a specific bug or regression, it seems to be just one example of an invalid scheme.\n\nShould we also consider adding a positive test for valid URL schemes? Perhaps we could use a template such as `Verify LDAP Config Update With Different URL Schemes`, where valid schemes are expected to return `204`/`200`, while invalid schemes are expected to return `400`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 140,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "c8383b84cd4b0423647a1d134ae8ec35c7bc16a3",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
