      "writtenOn": "2026-09-07T08:05:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that `ldapt://` is a valid negative case. However, similar to `Create LDAP Config With Various Port Numbers`, could we use a template to test multiple URL schemes here as well? \n\nFor example, we could cover several representative unsupported schemes with the expected `400` status. This would give us broader coverage of the URL scheme validation with only a small amount of additional test data and no significant maintenance overhead.\n\nThis also keeps the test consistent with the existing template-based approach used for other LDAP input validation cases.",
      "parentUuid": "7c250ae7_5d12ca46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 140,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "c8383b84cd4b0423647a1d134ae8ec35c7bc16a3",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
